<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Themed-icon layer (Android 13+). Same geometry as the foreground, but the
    colour is #FFFFFF because the system tints this layer itself from the
    user's wallpaper palette — a coloured monochrome layer comes out muddy,
    since the tint multiplies rather than replaces.

    Without this the launcher falls back to shrinking the full-colour icon
    into a grey circle when themed icons are on, which is where most apps
    look broken on a themed home screen.
-->
